# C8 reduced TS: OptTS + Freq in ONE job.
#
# `! OptTS Freq` runs the frequency calculation automatically at the converged
# saddle, in this job and this .out -- no second job, no geometry file to carry
# across. ORCA also refuses to run the Freq if the optimisation did not
# converge ("ORCA will abort at this point of the run"), so a frequency can
# never be read off an unconverged geometry. That guard is the reason to write
# it this way rather than as OptTS followed by a hand-copied NumFreq.
#
# Seed: frame 0 of ts/optts/job_trj.xyz -- the verified r2SCAN-3c TS (H135
# transferring, C129...O136 1.820) with its host relaxed at B97-3c. r2SCAN-3c
# and B97-3c are both 3c methods, so the QM region already sits in the B97-3c
# saddle's catchment; OptTS only refines it.
#
# ActiveAtoms + ExtendActiveRegion no hold the 120-atom host and move only the
# 17 QM atoms (2026-09-21 COMPUTATIONAL.md entry: %geom Cartesian constraints
# are the wrong layer here). Calc_Hess true gives OptTS the exact seed Hessian
# it needs to identify the imaginary mode; the trailing Freq recomputes the
# Hessian at the final geometry.
! QM/XTB B97-3c ddCOSMO(Water) OptTS Freq TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{61 64 120 121 122 124 125 126 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136}
END
ActiveAtoms
	{61 64 120 121 122 124 125 126 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136}
END
ExtendActiveRegion no
Charge_total 0
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%geom
  MaxIter 200
  Calc_Hess true
end

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job.xyz
